# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# .dockerignore uses its own matching rules, independent of .gitignore, and
# a bare pattern is not guaranteed to recurse into subdirectories - so
# "**/" prefixes are used below wherever a pattern must match at any depth.
# Every pattern here was checked against docker/api.Dockerfile,
# docker/mcp.Dockerfile and docker/web.Dockerfile to confirm it does not
# exclude anything those Dockerfiles actually COPY: gradlew, gradle/
# (including gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar), the module
# build.gradle.kts files, */src, and norintegrate-web's
# package.json/package-lock.json/source tree.

# VCS metadata: never a build input, and typically the single largest
# contributor to context size once a repo has commit history.
.git

# Node.js dependencies. Platform-specific native binaries built on the host
# (e.g. darwin-arm64 sharp/libvips) must never leak into a linux image.
# web.Dockerfile's deps stage runs its own `npm ci` for a musl-compatible
# copy inside the container; the host's norintegrate-web/node_modules is
# never a build input for any of the three Dockerfiles.
**/node_modules

# Next.js build/dev cache and static export output, regenerated by
# `npm run build` inside the builder stage - the host's macOS artifacts are
# irrelevant (and can be stale/incompatible).
**/.next
**/out

# Environment files may hold local secrets. No Dockerfile explicitly COPYs
# .env*, but web.Dockerfile's `COPY norintegrate-web/ .` would otherwise
# carry norintegrate-web/.env.local verbatim into the image. .env.example
# is a secret-free template, kept so it still works as reference/docs if a
# COPY ever needs it.
**/.env*
!**/.env.example

# Gradle/Kotlin build output and local caches. Not build inputs - the
# api/mcp Dockerfiles only COPY gradlew, the gradle/ wrapper directory
# (gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar included), build.gradle.kts /
# settings.gradle.kts, and each module's src/. These patterns match only a
# path segment literally named "build", ".gradle" or ".kotlin", so they do
# not touch build.gradle.kts files or the gradle/ wrapper directory.
**/build
**/.gradle
**/.kotlin

# IDE metadata
**/.idea
**/*.iml
**/*.iws

# OS metadata
**/.DS_Store

# Logs
**/*.log

# Frontend test/report artifacts, not build inputs.
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Terraform state can contain sensitive values; infra/ is never used as a
# build input for any of the three Dockerfiles.
infra/.terraform
infra/bootstrap/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
**/*.tfplan

# Agent tooling config and deployment manifests. Neither is a build input.
# .claude/settings.local.json is gitignored precisely because it is local
# and may hold machine-specific settings, so keep it out of the context too.
.claude
k8s
